# Optional overrides for `k dev`. Nothing here is needed: `k dev` at the
# workspace root wires paybox and the shop together, and shop/k.toml's [dev]
# section gives every other development value (SQLite in .k/, a generated
# admin password, the demo catalog, a local mail catcher). Copy to .env
# (git-ignored) only to change something; the process environment wins over
# .env, and .env over [dev]. See docs/design/25-config-and-secrets.md.

# Send confirmation email to Mailpit instead of the built-in catcher
# (`docker compose up --detach mail` at the workspace root, then open
# http://localhost:8025):
# SMTP_HOST=localhost
# SMTP_PORT=1025
# SMTP_SECURITY=none

# Use the admin password hash scripts/init-secrets.sh writes instead of a
# generated development password (relative paths are read from this
# directory):
# SHOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH_FILE=../secrets/admin_password_hash.txt

# Run the shop alone (`k dev --port 8081` here, with paybox already started
# by `k dev` in ../paybox): point it at paybox and share paybox's token,
# which ../paybox/.k/secrets/K_SERVICE_TOKEN holds once paybox has run.
# PAYBOX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# PAYBOX_TOKEN_FILE=../paybox/.k/secrets/K_SERVICE_TOKEN
# K_SERVICE_TOKEN_FILE=../paybox/.k/secrets/K_SERVICE_TOKEN

# No Stripe variables: Stripe is an optional binding, off by default (App.k).
